#X obj 595 11 hw.rpi.sensor.mpr121;
#X obj 230 93 cnv 1 535 325 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 98 The MPR121 is suitable for proximity detection and touch
sensing applications \, offering built-in electrode configuration \,
adjustable thresholds \, and filtering to ensure reliable performance
in noisy environments.;
#X text 240 168 If the @irq property is specified \, the sensor operates
in external interrupt mode \, and the specified GPIO pin is taken for
exclusive use and is unavailable to other objects.;
#X obj 230 173 cnv 1 2 60 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -260289 -1 0;
#X text 240 238 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 263 • Capacitive touch interfaces — building a 12-key touch
keyboard \, a touch-sensitive control panel or a custom musical interface
\, where each electrode corresponds to a note \, parameter or action.;
#X text 250 333 • Interactive installations with physical touch — connecting
conductive objects (fruit \, plants \, metal surfaces) to the electrodes
\, so the audience can trigger sounds or changes in the installation
by touching them.;
